HTTP REQUEST TYPES:
GET, POST(CREATE), DELETE, PUT(UPDATE)

HTTP RESPONSE TYPES:
2xx - OK (Successful)
3xx - Redirection
4xx - Client Errors
5xx - Server Errors

MOCK BACKEND API:
mock api -> mockoon

HTTPCLIENT AND OBSERVABLES:
 - to send http request and wait for result from backend
    - Add HttpClientModule to app.module.ts "import {HttpClientModule} from '@angular/common/http';"
    - import { HttpClient } from '@angular/common/http'; in our reservation service
    - import { Observable } from 'rxjs';

Observable:
    - its an asynchronous way on how we can wait for a result
    - every request we send to external api might take some time to respond
    - we create a observale, [ we send the request out and we are waiting ]
    - every method that calls the method which returns obervable subscribes to the observale just like an event.
    - we subsribe to it and wait for the result
    - once the request is processed and we get the result, everyone who subscribed to the Observable will get notified and move forward with result.
    
    All methods that call getReservation will subsribe to the Observal that can return Reservation array
    getReservations(): Observable<Reservation[]>{
            // return this.reservations;
            return this.http.get<Reservation[]>(this.apiUrl + "/reservations")
        }
    Reservation-list.component.ts:
        ngOnInit(): void {
            this.reservationService.getReservations().subscribe( reservations => {
                this.reservations = reservations
            });
         }
